WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.256
Selling on Amazon can be broken down into four steps.

00:00:05.256 --> 00:00:06.307
Step 1.

00:00:06.307 --> 00:00:10.512
Create an Amazon Seller Central account on sell.

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:11.038
amazon.

00:00:11.038 --> 00:00:11.564
com.

00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:12.615
Step 2.

00:00:12.615 --> 00:00:14.717
List Products for Sale.

00:00:14.717 --> 00:00:15.768
Step 3.

00:00:15.768 --> 00:00:19.973
Fulfill Customer Orders and Provide Outstanding Customer Service.

00:00:19.973 --> 00:00:21.025
Step 4.

00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:26.806
Receive payments from your sales proceeds and maintain your account health.

00:00:26.806 --> 00:00:29.960
Let's go over these four steps.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.215
Step 1.

00:00:31.215 --> 00:00:34.860
Create an Amazon Seller Central Account.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.720
Before you register for an account with Amazon,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.362
choose between professional or individual selling plan.

00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:45.760
Confused on which plan is right for your business?

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.137
There are a few important differences.

00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:51.389
Between the two plans.

00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:52.514
Let's compare.

00:00:52.514 --> 00:00:53.640
Professional accounts

00:00:53.640 --> 00:01:00.716
carry a flat monthly subscription fee of $39.99 no matter how many items you sell.

00:01:00.716 --> 00:01:01.660
This type

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.820
of account makes sense if you're planning to sell a lot of items.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:06.780
An individual account

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.885
is a better choice if you only plan to make a few sales each month.

00:01:10.885 --> 00:01:11.980
Instead of a flat

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:17.947
monthly subscription fee, you pay a per item fee of $0.99 for every item you sell.

00:01:17.947 --> 00:01:18.320
Both

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.766
individual and professional seller accounts are eligible for FBA service.

00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:24.100
Now let's take

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.836
a look at the features which are only available for professional selling account.

00:01:28.836 --> 00:01:29.200
Customized

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.633
shipping rates.

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:32.783
Bulk listing tools.

00:01:32.783 --> 00:01:35.650
Advertising, deals and coupons.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.800
Automated pricing tools.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.165
Amazon Selling Coach.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.895
Marketplace web services and much more.

00:01:41.895 --> 00:01:44.625
Now let's look at Step 2.

00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:45.080
List

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:45.478
products.

00:01:45.478 --> 00:01:51.045
You can list a product to sell on Amazon in less than five minutes.

00:01:51.045 --> 00:01:51.840
Here's how.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.240
Amazon's product listing allows sellers to match an existing listing.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.600
If someone is already

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.539
selling the same product or create a new listing if you are the first or only seller.

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:02.120
If you

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:07.480
are reselling products already present in Amazon's catalog, this can be a fast way to add selection

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.740
to your account.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:12.520
What if my selection doesn't match the existing offers?

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.200
If you are selling

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.920
your own brand, private label, or bringing new product selections to a category, you'll

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.482
want to create a new detail page on Amazon.

00:02:23.482 --> 00:02:27.440
To create a new listing, you will need a product

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.074
identifier, also known as a barcode.

00:02:31.074 --> 00:02:35.920
Commonly used identifier terms include UPC, GTIN, EAN

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.579
or ISBN.

00:02:36.579 --> 00:02:38.885
Not exactly sure what a barcode is.

00:02:38.885 --> 00:02:41.520
Look for barcodes on some of your favorite

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.381
items or watch what a clerk scans to get a price in a store.

00:02:45.381 --> 00:02:46.760
Look at the numbers printed

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.762
below the barcode.

00:02:47.762 --> 00:02:52.772
A 12-digit number is a UPC or a 13-digit number is an EAN.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.440
If the

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.828
products you intend to sell do not have a barcode.

00:02:56.828 --> 00:02:58.522
Apply for a GTIN exemption.

00:02:58.522 --> 00:02:59.200
You can

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.747
then add the selection without the need for barcode numbers.

00:03:02.747 --> 00:03:04.520
Add listings to your account,

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.860
one by one using the add a product option.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:11.200
Add bulk inventory all at once by using the

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.097
add products via upload option.

00:03:14.097 --> 00:03:17.960
Special listing options cater to the unique demands

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.394
of handmade and customizable listing sellers.

00:03:21.394 --> 00:03:25.400
Step three, fulfill orders and provide outstanding

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.221
customer service.

00:03:26.221 --> 00:03:31.560
Now that your product listings are complete, choose how to best fulfill orders.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.360
The FBA program gives sellers the opportunity to use Amazon's world-class shipping, logistics

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.766
and customer service partnerships to benefit their buyers.

00:03:41.766 --> 00:03:44.520
Sellers using FBA send their

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.103
products to Amazon's fulfillment centers.

00:03:48.103 --> 00:03:53.120
We take care of packaging, shipping, returns

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.063
and customer service issues.

00:03:55.063 --> 00:03:59.434
Products are prime enabled with a prime badge logo.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:03:59.920
Sellers

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.020
that prefer to do their own or merchant fulfilled shipping are responsible for packages being

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:10.330
shipped and delivered on time, customer service and returns.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.280
Step four, receive payments from

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.437
your sales proceeds.

00:04:14.437 --> 00:04:18.680
Amazon pays you through an automatic clearing house payment to your

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:22.589
bank account every two weeks on eligible sales proceeds.

00:04:22.589 --> 00:04:24.760
To determine sales proceeds and

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.200
profitability, sellers should become familiar with Amazon's fee schedule.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.680
On your Seller

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:35.127
Central home page, type in selling on Amazon fee schedule in the search bar.

00:04:35.127 --> 00:04:36.080
This will direct

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.798
you to the help page.

00:04:37.798 --> 00:04:41.576
The help page lists all fees related to selling on Amazon.

00:04:41.576 --> 00:04:41.920
Lastly,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:47.120
we recommend you to visit account health under the performance tab on seller central to regularly

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.248
monitor your performance as a seller.

00:04:49.248 --> 00:04:52.085
This wraps up how selling on Amazon works.

00:04:52.085 --> 00:04:52.440
Thank

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.200
you, and happy selling!
